Better approach: for local dev/preview, run a Node/Bun WebSocket server locally and preview it. The user wants to play over network — multiple devices connecting. Options:

1. Node.js server (ws library) + static HTML, run locally with `preview` — devices on same LAN can join.
2. Cloudflare Worker with Durable Objects — can't easily deploy via sites_deploy manifest (needs DO bindings).

Given the guidance: "Before even a preview deployment, build and test locally" — and hosting isn't explicitly requested. The user asked for a game, multiplayer over network. The simplest robust thing: a single Node/Bun server serving static files + WebSocket endpoint (using plain `ws` or built-in). Then run it locally, register preview, and tell the user their friends on the same Wi-Fi can join via LAN IP.

