Game design (word party game, multiplayer):
- Host creates room with 4-6 letter code.
- Players join with name from phone browser.
- Game: all get same secret word (e.g., from a category), except impostor gets a different/random one (or "IMPOSTER" with no word).
- Rounds: each player gives a one-word clue describing the word, in turn order. Impostor tries to blend in.
- After clues, discussion (optional), then voting: each player votes for who they think is the impostor.
- If impostor gets most votes → crew win. Impostor also gets a chance to guess the word (or gets extra turn to guess after voting?) Classic rules: if impostor survives the vote, they get one chance to guess the word; correct guess = impostor wins.
- Reveal.

Keep it well-scoped but polished: nice dark UI, phone-friendly, lobby with player list, host controls (start game, settings for # players, category).

