{"kind":"tool","id":"QjJ3vaOfAvQ","toolName":"write_file","input":{"path":"README.md","instructions":"Create a README documenting how to run and play the impostor game","content":"# 🕵️ IMPOSTER

A real-time, multiplayer **word party game** for 3–12 players — the impostor game.

Everyone gets the **same secret word**… except one player, who secretly gets a
**different word from the same category**. Give one-word clues, argue about who
doesn't belong, and vote them out. If the impostor survives the vote, they get
one guess at the real word to steal the win.

## Run it

```bash
npm install   # just the `ws` WebSocket library
npm start     # serves the game on http://localhost:5173
```

Then open `http://localhost:5173`, create a room, and share the **4-letter room
code**. Friends on the same Wi-Fi join by opening the LAN address shown in the
lobby (e.g. `http://10.200.34.43:5173`) and entering the code.

```bash
npm test      # end-to-end test: plays two full rounds over real WebSockets
```

Set `PORT` to serve on a different port.

## Rounds

1. **Deal** — crew all get the same word; the impostor gets a different one.
2. **Clues** — one word per player, in turn order. Crew may not say the word itself.
3. **Discuss** — 60 seconds of chat and accusations (host can cut it short).
4. **Vote** — one vote each. Ties and skips mean nobody is eliminated.
5. **Finish** — impostor voted out → crew wins. Otherwise the impostor picks the
   real word from three options → impostor wins.

## Layout

- [server.js](server.js) — HTTP + WebSocket server, rooms, and the game state machine
- [public/index.html](public/index.html), [public/app.js](public/app.js), [public/style.css](public/style.css) — the phone-friendly client
- [test/e2e.mjs](test/e2e.mjs) — plays two complete rounds and asserts the whole flow

Rooms live in memory: restart the server and the rooms are gone (players are
offered the home screen and can create or join again).
