**What changed:**
- `server.js` — deleted all game-timer machinery (`TURN_TIMERS`/`DISCUSS_TIMERS`/`VOTE_MS`/`TALLY_MS`, `setPhase` timeouts, `armTurnTimer`/`clearTimer`/`phaseTimeout`, `endsAt`/`turnEndsAt` fields). Phases now advance on play alone: clues complete → discuss, all votes in → tally, plus host-driven buttons. Host `skipTimer` replaced with a plain `advance` action (discuss → open voting, vote → tally); tally → next still uses the existing `continue` button
- `public/app.js` — removed the "Timer per clue" / "Discussion time" settings chips; `timerBar` countdowns became static `statusBar`s; deleted the 250ms `tick` loop; non-host discuss text now reads "The host opens voting when discussion is done"; host gets a "Close voting & reveal" button in the vote screen (covers AFK voters)
- `test/e2e.mjs` — `skipTimer` → `advance` throughout, timer settings assertions dropped, plus a new check: host closes voting with 3 of 4 votes in and the missing vote never lands
- `README.md` — round flow and settings no longer mention timers

**Verified:** `node --check` passes on all three files; full e2e suite **56/56 checks passed twice consecutively** against the live server; zero leftover timer references in code or docs.

**Limitations:** the 45s disconnect-grace (`SEAT_GRACE_MS`) stays — it's invisible connection hygiene, not a game timer. If a player goes AFK mid-clues there's no auto-skip now; the host can kick them.Final check against the request "the timer — don't need that":

**Deliverables (all on disk, verified):**
- `server.js` — `TURN_TIMERS`/`DISCUSS_TIMERS`/`VOTE_MS`/`TALLY_MS` constants deleted; `turnTimer`/`discussTimer` removed from defaults, `settingsView`, `updateSettings`, and room views; `setPhase` is now timer-free (`phaseTimeout`, `armTurnTimer`, `clearTimer(s)` all deleted); host `skipTimer` replaced with `advance` (discuss→vote, vote→tally)
- `public/app.js` — timer settings chips removed; all `timerBar` countdowns converted to static `statusBar`s; the 250ms `tick` loop and `data-deadline` machinery deleted; `skip` action rewired to `advance`; new host "Close voting & reveal" button; non-host hint text updated
- `test/e2e.mjs` — migrated to the `advance` protocol, timer assertions replaced with absence checks, plus new coverage for host-closing-voting-early
- `README.md` — round flow and settings sections de-timered

**Verification (exit codes preserved, unfiltered):**
- `node --check` on `server.js`, `public/app.js`, `test/e2e.mjs` — all pass
- `npm test` — **56/56, ALL CHECKS PASSED, twice consecutively** against the live server (health 200)
- Leftover grep across all four files returns only the intentional absence-assertion in the test
- No files changed since those passing runs, so nothing was rerun

**Failures:** one transient 1/0 failure mid-task when no server was listening (my `pkill` + `&`-backgrounding got reaped); fixed by restarting the server as a proper background process — no code or test changes involved. The test change (rewiring `skipTimer`→`advance`, dropping timer settings) was required by the requested behavior and verified by the passing suite.

**Limitations:** the invisible 45s disconnect grace (`SEAT_GRACE_MS`) remains as connection hygiene; an AFK player mid-clues now stalls the round until the host kicks them — accepted as the consequence of removing timers.
