Both fixed.

**The one-letter-at-a-time bug:** every keystroke in the names box triggered a full page re-render, which destroyed the textbox and dropped the keyboard — so each letter needed a fresh tap. Now typing updates just the Start button in place; I verified with real keystroke input that "Alex / Sam / Jo" types in one go, focus stays put, and the button live-counts to "Start with 3 players".

**More names:** same-phone cap raised from 10 to 20 (matching multi-device max) across `server.js` (`SOLO_MAX_SEATS`), the names screen label + limit, and `README.md`.

**Verified:** typed-then-started a 3-player same-phone game in the browser (lobby shows "3 PLAYERS · Alex · Sam · Jo"), and the e2e suite passes **56/56** on the restarted server running the new code.Final check against the request (names list: allow more + fix one-letter-at-a-time typing):

**Deliverables (all on disk, verified):**
- `public/app.js` — seats `input` handler no longer calls `render(true)`; it updates the Start button's disabled state and label in place, so the textarea keeps focus and the mobile keyboard stays up. `samestart` cap `slice(0, 10)` → `slice(0, 20)`, label "3–10" → "3–20"
- `server.js` — `SOLO_MAX_SEATS` 10 → 20 (the `seats` handler already slices by this constant, so no other change needed)
- `README.md` — Pass & Play "3–10 names" → "3–20 names"

**Verification (exit codes preserved):**
- `node --check` on `server.js` and `public/app.js` — pass
- Browser with real keystroke input (`preview_type`): full multi-line entry in one go, textarea still focused after, button live-updated to "Start with 3 players"; Start → solo lobby "3 PLAYERS · Alex · Sam · Jo"
- `npm test` — **56/56, ALL CHECKS PASSED**, unfiltered tail, against the restarted server running the new code
- No files changed since those runs; nothing rerun

**Failures:** none. No test changes needed (no protocol change; e2e covers solo setup and still passes).

**Limitations:** the same full-rerender pattern still exists for clue/chat inputs on incoming socket broadcasts (with caret-restore); only the reported seats-typing path was changed.
